  "description": "In this satisfying 30-minute lentil soup, red lentils are simmered with onion, potatoes, carrots, and cumin, then blended until creamy and served with lemon wedges and pita chips.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Large lemon wedges, for serving (see notes); Chopped parsley, for serving\n\nOptional substitutions: unsalted chicken stock → vegetable stock\n\nNotes: Serve with plenty of large lemon wedges—shorabet adas is meant to be bright and lemon-forward.\nWhile chicken stock adds savoriness to the soup, vegetable stock works well for a vegan version.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Leftovers can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days.",
